The sidebar is a tree, not a row of play buttons
===============================================

The first attempt was wrong in every way that matters. The caret was a floating shape inside the row
rather than a control in its own column, so labels did not line up. It pointed right, so it read as
"play" instead of "opens downward". The whole row was not a hit target. Children rendered as solid
blocks stacked vertically. And the Tools & skills section opened to nothing, because it listed skills
that are not loaded at the time the sidebar draws.

Now:

  * the caret lives in a fixed 26px gutter, so every label starts on the same column
  * closed points DOWN (it opens downward), open flips UP (it closes upward)
  * the entire row is the hit target, and the open row carries a tinted band
  * children indent under a guide rail as full-width rows, selectable with up/down arrow keys
  * Tools & skills lists configured connections first — the things that actually exist when the
    sidebar draws — then skills, and does not open to an empty box

